# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the GizmoSQL integration suite
# (.github/workflows/tsan.yml, TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp).
#
# Keep this list short and justified. Every entry hides a report, so each must
# name a known-benign pattern in third-party code, with the reason, and never a
# GizmoSQL symbol: a race in src/ is a bug to fix, not to suppress. Syntax:
#   race:<symbol or file substring>   thread_leak:<...>   deadlock:<...>
# See https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions

# DuckDB storage engine: a transaction commit appends rows into a transient
# column segment (ColumnSegment::Append) while another pipeline thread scans the
# same segment. DuckDB's MVCC design publishes the committed row count under the
# row group lock and readers never look past it, so the overlapping bytes are
# never observed; TSan cannot see that invariant. Reported at
# validity_uncompressed.cpp (ValidityAppend vs ValidityScan) in the integration
# suite; the same pattern exists for every compression function's Append.
race:duckdb::ColumnSegment::Append


# DuckDB hash join: parallel probe threads set one-byte "found match" markers in
# the shared hash table (ScanStructure::NextInnerJoin, NextRightSemiOrAntiJoin)
# for right/outer/semi/anti joins. Every writer stores the same value, so the
# outcome is identical regardless of ordering; DuckDB relies on that instead of
# atomics. Reported under concurrent TPC-H queries.
race:duckdb::JoinHashTable::ScanStructure

# jemalloc (bundled by DuckDB): its extent metadata is managed with its own
# atomics and lock-free structures that TSan cannot model, so it reports races
# inside jemalloc/internal/edata.h on every allocation-heavy run. Standard
# jemalloc suppression; no GizmoSQL frame is involved.
race:third_party/jemalloc

# GDAL, inside DuckDB's spatial extension: registering the module takes its
# global bootstrap mutex and a per-object mutex in both orders
# (CPLCreateOrAcquireMutexEx vs CPLAcquireMutex) while single-threaded at load
# time. TSan reports the cycle as a potential deadlock; both stacks are GDAL.
deadlock:duckdb::RegisterGDALModule
